The most recent Volkswagen Tiguan TSI eHybrid is part of the third generation (Mk3), available from late 2023/early 2024. It comes in two power outputs: 204 PS (201 HP) and 272 PS (268 HP). It uses a 1.5-litre TSI petrol engine paired with an electric motor and a larger 19.7 kWh (usable) or 25.7 kWh (total) battery.

